verifiers.killer:
The right can be bought, but never cheaply relative to its proven value. Every standard way to acquire land near a settlement fixes the landowner's share of the uplift in the contract:
- promotion agreements leave 80-95% of the consented value with the landowner, with minimum-price vetoes;
- options are priced at market value at exercise, less only a 10-30% discount;
- outright sales of land next to a settlement routinely carry 25-35% overage on any planning uplift for 10-30 years.

Owners are also actively told about grey-belt potential by promoters (Richborough brochures), consultants (Turley) and agents (Bidwells). So ML-led site picking cannot create a purchase spread that informed buyers miss. The only lever left is a 1.1-1.3x hit-rate edge on a proving step whose base rate is already 55-80%.
